{{#is_alert}}
## What's happening?
Collector receiver `{{receiver.name}}` refused **{{value}} log records** during the last 15 minutes, so clients are getting HTTP 503 or gRPC UNAVAILABLE back. This signal is also shared across destinations: the receiver sits upstream of the exporter fan-out, so it cannot attribute the pressure to the BYOC path on its own. It only fires for pushed input. A `filelog` receiver has no caller to refuse, so this metric stays flat on file-tailing pipelines even under heavy pressure.
{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_recovery}}Receiver `{{receiver.name}}` stopped refusing log records.{{/is_recovery}}

